From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the engine vendors Brave's filter engine

adblock 0.13.6 filters requests and pages for the engine's content
blocking. Its features are full-regex-handling and single-thread, with
no default features: the embedded domain resolver needs the addr crate,
and the engine resolves domains from net instead.

It brings twelve crates Chromium lacks, which are new files under
third_party/rust. Three only build: thiserror-impl, and semver and
rustc_version for flatbuffers' build script. Here regex ships, since adblock matches with it in the
browser, and bitflags gains serde for adblock's filter masks. thiserror
is configured by epoch, since thiserror 1 writes no private.rs.
